<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_appendix"><a href="#A7" title="In Self-Jailbreaking: Language Models Can Reason Themselves Out of Safety Alignment After Benign Reasoning Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">G </span>Relationship between Compliant and Perceived Harmfulness Directions</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_appendix"><a href="#A8" title="In Self-Jailbreaking: Language Models Can Reason Themselves Out of Safety Alignment After Benign Reasoning Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">H </span>Projection Scores on Perceived Harmfulness Direction</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_appendix"><a href="#A9" title="In Self-Jailbreaking: Language Models Can Reason Themselves Out of Safety Alignment After Benign Reasoning Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">I </span>STAR-1 Safety Reasoning Example</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_appendix"><a href="#A10" title="In Self-Jailbreaking: Language Models Can Reason Themselves Out of Safety Alignment After Benign Reasoning Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">J </span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Safe-s1.1-7B</span>: Example Output and Compliance Score</span></a></li>
</ol></nav>
